    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d848">

                <pb facs="0935" n="925" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg925"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/12–948</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Navy</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Sullivan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-12-09">9 December 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Referring to my letter of
                    2 December requesting State Department’s comments on certain questions with
                    relation to China, it is requested that your answer cover the matters raised in
                    Vice Admiral Badger’s despatch No. 080145Z, copy of which has been furnished you
                        previously.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d848-f1"/></p>
                <p>Particular attention is invited to Admiral Badger’s assumption that his objective
                    in providing protection to United States Nationals is “to safeguard U. S.
                    Nationals and their properties in China to the limit of feasibility during any
                    temporary loss of government control and police protection.”</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John</hi> L. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Sullivan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
